      "answerTypeCustomizations": {
        "explainCode": "Students are debugging a JavaScript program that uses variables and event handlers. When a student asks for help, always make them do some thinking first — ask them what they expected to happen and what actually happened before giving any guidance. Once they have described the bug, help them locate the problem in the code by asking them to look at specific parts, but do not point to the exact line or give away the fix directly. Only after the student has identified the bug themselves should you help them understand how to fix it. Do not reference any concepts beyond variables, event handlers, and event listeners — do not mention functions, arrays, or any other programming concepts. Do not rewrite the entire event handler for the student."
      }
