        "15": {
          "id": "15",
          "name": "triage.md",
          "contents": "Bug Triage\n\nBug 1\n\nWhat I observed:\nSeverity (high / medium / low):\nMy hypothesis:\n\n---\n\nBug 2\n\nWhat I observed:\nSeverity (high / medium / low):\nMy hypothesis:\n\n---\n\nBug 3\n\nWhat I observed:\nSeverity (high / medium / low):\nMy hypothesis:\n\n---\n\nBug 4\n\nWhat I observed:\nSeverity (high / medium / low):\nMy hypothesis:\n\n---\n\nBug 5\n\nWhat I observed:\nSeverity (high / medium / low):\nMy hypothesis:\n\n---\n\nFix order\n\nI'll fix these in this order:\n\n1.\n2.\n3.\n\nBecause:\n",
          "folderId": "0",
          "active": true
        }
      },
      "openFiles": [
        "15",
        "3"
      ]
    },
    "long_instructions": "## Do This:\r\n\r\nYou're a QA Engineer at FitTrack, a fitness app. Your manager just messaged you:\r\n\r\n> \"Five bugs reported on the stats tracker this morning. Triage them, then fix in order of severity. Track your work in triage.md.\"\r\n\r\n1. Open `triage.md`. Click each button and observe how the stats change. For each bug you find, note what happened and rate the severity (high, medium, low).\r\n\r\n2. Based on your notes, decide what order to fix the bugs in.\r\n\r\n3. For each bug, write your best guess: which variable is wrong, and what do you think the bug is? Then share your observation and your guess with AI Tutor and ask for help finding and fixing it.\r\n\r\n4. Fix the code in `script.js` and test again until all five buttons work as expected.",
    "display_name": "Fitness Tracker",
    "thumbnail_url": "https://images.code.org/24177b03713b2006ef202dfc46f85ac9-steps-icon.png",
    "bubble_choice_description": "Track steps, water, and workout streaks as you interact with the app. Debug how each action updates your daily fitness progress.",
